# Canonical author identities.
#
# Four people committed under nine different names and addresses, because git
# identities were not configured consistently across machines and because one
# member's assistant tooling wrote commits under its own name. This file maps
# every variant onto one identity per person, so `git shortlog -sne`, `git log`
# and the GitHub contributors graph report contribution per person rather than
# per laptop.
#
# It renames nothing in history; it is a lookup applied when authorship is read.
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical-email> <commit-email>

